### Insurance Coverage and Sliding Scale Fees

Insurance can make mental health care more manageable, so it is smart to ask early which plans a practice accepts. Some providers in the area list a wide range of insurance options, while others may help you understand what out-of-network reimbursement could look like. That first call can answer a lot.

Not every practice publicly lists sliding scale options, so ask directly if lower-cost arrangements are available. Even when sliding scale is not offered, intake staff and other health care professionals can explain alternatives, including telehealth or provider matching based on your budget and goals.

Questions worth asking include:

- Is this counselor in-network with my insurance plan?
- Are sliding scale or reduced-fee appointments available?
- Are telehealth sessions an option if I need flexibility?

